RTATTRIB pair=rt_hip_device_vs_rt_hip_hostpath r1_fields_bit_identical=True wcast_bit_identical=True every_moving_slot_has_a_moving_probs_addend=True fields_moving_outside_the_exp_path=none premise_ulp_to_pinned_pre_cast=4/2 (band 5) zero_tolerance_ndiff=ids=0/8,ids_alt=0/8,wcast=0/8 verdict=CONSISTENT-WITH-R5-EXP-SCOPE note=§R5 predicts exactly this shape: R1 identical, `probs` moved by the two libms' exp(), `wpre` moved inside that scope, `wcast` identical because the bf16 cast absorbs it, `wleak` identical because both arms round R1 to the same bf16 before renormalising. If any of those four fails the difference is not the documented scope and the fix belongs in the kernel, not in this check
